course: dictionary
lesson: 3727
title: Flipper: one word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Read the words around it first. «Humpbacks have the longest flippers of any whale» is about animals, so here a flipper is a flat, wide limb used for swimming.
explain: Now read «Flippers are long rubber shoes like fins that people wear on their feet to swim faster.» These are not animal limbs. The words people, rubber and feet show that this is the second meaning. Check by swapping the meaning into the sentence: «people wear rubber fins on their feet» still makes sense, so you have the right one.
explain: Clues can be small. «Sea turtles cannot pull their heads or flippers into their shells» tells you that a flipper is part of the body, because it is pulled in along with the head. Some flippers do more than swim: sea lions can walk on all four flippers.
fact: A flipper is a flat, wide limb that seals, turtles, penguins and dolphins use for swimming.
fact: Flippers are also long rubber shoes, like fins, that people wear on their feet to swim faster.
fact: Humpback whales have the longest flippers of any whale, about a third of their body length.
fact: On land penguins waddle, but in the water their wings have become stiff flippers.
fact: The same word names the body part and the swimming shoe, so the context tells you which one is meant.
exercise: «Humpbacks have the longest flippers of any whale.» In this sentence, what is a flipper? | *A flat, wide limb used for swimming | A type of fin on a boat | A tail that splashes | A long rubber shoe for swimming
exercise: «Flippers are long rubber shoes like fins that people wear on their feet.» What are flippers in this sentence? | Hard shells on a turtle | Bumps on a whale's front edge | Animal limbs for swimming | *Long rubber shoes for swimming faster
exercise: «Sea turtles cannot pull their heads or flippers into their shells.» What does this sentence tell you about flippers? | They are bumps on the front edge of a whale | *They are body parts that can be pulled into the shell | They are rubber shoes worn by people | They are used only to fly
test: «Galápagos sea lions, which have four flippers, nap on benches and boats.» What is a flipper in this sentence? | A kind of boat | A bump on a whale | A rubber shoe worn to swim faster | *A limb of the body, used for swimming and walking
test: «He wore flippers to snorkel in the bay.» Which meaning fits best? | Ear flaps on a seal | *Rubber shoes for swimming faster | A stiff wing of a penguin | A limb of an animal
exam: «On land penguins waddle like clumsy toys, but in the water their wings have become stiff flippers.» What does this show about the penguin's wings? | They are made of rubber shoes | They are shells that protect the body | *They have turned into flippers for swimming | Wings are used only to fly
